= M.U.L.E.

The classic game of settling the planet Irata, for four colonists on any
FujiNet machine at all -- the other three may be on an Atari computer, an
Apple, a PC, an Intellivision or another 2600, and the computer takes any
empty seat. Twelve months to claim land, outfit your M.U.L.E.s, and trade your
way to the richest colony.

#shots(("mule-02-lobby", [The colony room]), ("mule-08-develop-town", [The town]),
       ("mule-09-develop-map", [The map]), h: 1.0in)

== Loading the Game

Choose *M.U.L.E.* and the room *Planet IRATA* in the Lobby, or load it from
the browser: host *apps.irata.online*, folder *mule*, then *atari-2600*, game
*MULE2600.BIN*. On the title screen press the red button (*FIRE: START*),
give your name if it asks, and pick a table (*FIRE: JOIN*; *RIGHT: RELOAD*
fetches the list again). In the colony room, choose your race with the
joystick and press the red button when you are ready.

#controls(title: [M.U.L.E.],
  [Joystick], [Walk; choose; move your auction line; declare (up to sell, down to buy).],
  [#FIRE], [Start, join and ready; claim a plot; begin your turn; install a M.U.L.E., take a sample, catch the Wampus; collude; sit out a declaration.],
  [#SELECT], [End your turn.],
  [#RESET held for a second], [Leave the table. The computer takes over your colonist.],
  [#key("LEFT DIFFICULTY") at A], [Sound off.],
)

The 2600 draws the map and the town with letters. On the map, *F*, *E*, *S*
and *C* are Food, Energy, Smithore and Crystite M.U.L.E.s, and each owner's
colour frames their land. In the town, *C S E F* are the outfitters and *A L
P* the assay office, the land office and the pub. Messages run along the
bottom line.

#rules[The whole game -- the colonists, the land, every phase of a month, the
auctions, every fortune and catastrophe -- is in the _M.U.L.E. Player's
Guide_, Atari 2600 edition, from the FujiNet project.]
